i'm not looking at the spoilers or code at the moment but keep this
in mind: artifact bonuses are added to what a weapon might normally
do.  also the damage is a random number whose range is somewhat
indicated by the number you see in the spoiler file.

[] Lawful characters get Excalibur (+10 damage) AND Mjollnir (+24
[] damage!).  Excalibur protects agains level drains and helps with
[] searching.

Excalibur gives an additional random damage upto 10 over what a
long sword might normally do (i believe that's a random number
whose max is 12).  Mjollnir gives a random damage upto 24 over
what a war hammer might do (i think that's max 4).  so Mjollnir
is only marginally better in this respect.

[] What do Neutral characters get?  A few swords that add +5 to hit, but
[] otherwise do no extra damage, and don't even work on everything
[] (Giantslayer does no extra damage, and only gives "to hit" bonuses on
[] giants).  I'm assuming that when the spoiler file says +5, +0, it
[] means that it's +5 to hit, and +0 to damage.

if you hadn't read the spoilers and simply used the weapons you
wouldn't feel this way ...

the 0 on damage translates into 2x damage (relative to what the
weapon might normally do).  Fire Brand (effective on all but
fire resistant and similarly for Frost Brand) gives a random
damage upto 2x12=24, so Foo Brand is equivalent to Stormy and
Mojo in this respect.

[] Granted, neutral characters can (possibly) get Stormbringer by
[] praying ...

no, i think neutrals and lawfuls get Excalibur and chaotics alone
get Stormbringer this way.

